      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T21:40:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My main use case is running multiple NFS-Ganesha instances on the same storage node, each bound to its own VIP, while sharing the same physical RoCE-capable NIC.\n\nI want each instance to listen on its assigned VIP instead of 0.0.0.0, allowing multiple instances to use the same NFS/RDMA port without wildcard listener conflicts.\n\nI understand your concern about restricting a listener to a single RDMA device. In my use case, that restriction is intentional.\n\nTo preserve the existing behavior for multi-interface deployments, I can introduce a separate RDMA bind address parameter that defaults to 0.0.0.0.",
