      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T16:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, there\u0027s no need for a separate RDMA-specific bind parameter since Bind_Addr already defaults to a wildcard address.\n\nI\u0027ve also tested the proposed change with multiple NFS-Ganesha instances running on the same host, each bound to a different VIP and using the same NFS/RDMA port (20049). This works as expected.\n\nThe patch simply extends the existing Bind_Addr behavior to the RDMA listener, preserving wildcard binding by default while allowing explicit per-IP binding when needed.\n\nI believe this addresses the concern without introducing additional configuration options. Please let me know if there\u0027s anything else you\u0027d like me to change before merging.",
